        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "flattenReqs",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "/* ---------------------------------------------------------\n   DATA PREPARATION NODE\n   Parses raw Requisition JSON strings and extracts key fields\n--------------------------------------------------------- */\n\n// 1. Get the raw input\nvar rawInput = $context.$nodes.GETREQUISITIONDETAILSFORALLREQS.$output;\n\nvar simplifiedReqs = [];\n\n// 2. Iterate and Extract\nif (rawInput && Array.isArray(rawInput)) {\n    for (var i = 0; i < rawInput.length; i++) {\n        var itemStr = rawInput[i];\n\n        try {\n            // The input is an array of JSON strings, so we must parse each one\n            var req = JSON.parse(itemStr);\n\n            // Logic: Prefer External Description, fallback to Internal\n            var finalDesc = req.InternalDescription;\n            if (req.ExternalDescription && req.ExternalDescription.length > 0) {\n                finalDesc = req.ExternalDescription;\n            }\n\n            // Build the clean object\n            simplifiedReqs.push({\n                \"requisitionId\": req.RequisitionId,\n                \"reqTitle\": req.Title,\n                \"location\": req.PrimaryLocationName,\n                \"description\": finalDesc\n            });\n\n        } catch (e) {\n            // Skip invalid items\n            continue;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// 3. Prepare Output\nvar finalOutput = {\n    \"llmInputList\": simplifiedReqs\n};\n\nreturn finalOutput;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765242883247"
          },
          "code": "FLATTENREQS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1765223967281",
          "id": "1765333394436",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "convertReqsToSearchCriteria"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765312509749"
          },
          "code": "CONVERTREQSTOSEARCHCRITERIA",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1765223967281",
          "id": "1765242883247",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765242883248_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "*** SYSTEM INSTRUCTIONS ***\nYou are a strict JSON data transformation engine. \nYou will receive an input array of requisition objects. \nYour goal is to process EVERY item in the input array and return a SINGLE valid JSON object containing all results.\nDo not output markdown formatting (like ```json). \nDo not output conversational text. \nReturn ONLY the raw JSON string.\n\n*** INPUT DATA ***\n {{$context.$nodes.GETREQUISITIONDETAILSFORALLREQS.$output}} \n\n*** PROCESSING RULES ***\n\nFor EACH item in the input array, perform the following:\n\n1. ID EXTRACTION: \n   - Extract the ID from `result.RequisitionId` (or `result.requisitionId`). Map this to \"requisitionId\".\n\n2. TITLE EXTRACTION:\n   - Extract the title from `result.Title` (or `result.title`). Map this to \"ReqTitle\".\n   - If the title is null/empty, set \"ReqTitle\" to \"N/A\".\n\n3. SEARCH CRITERIA GENERATION:\n   - Analyze `result.description` and `result.shortDescription`.\n   - Generate a single string formatted EXACTLY as: Skills: [A, B]; Degree: [C]\n   - Rules for SearchCriteria:\n     - \"Skills\": Extract 5-7 distinct, hard skills (short values, wrapped in double quotes).\n     - \"Degree\": Extract required degrees (wrapped in double quotes). If none found, omit the Degree section. Degree can also include High School Diploma etc\n     - Do NOT populate age in Degree: [At least 18 years of age]. Degree mean educational degrees from schools, colleges etc\n     - Include JobTitles and a few synonyms relevant to the requisiition\n     - The total length of this string must be ≤ 450 characters.\n     - FORMAT EXAMPLE: Skills: [<Skill A>, <Skill B>, <Skill C>]; Degree: [<Degree Name>], JobTitle: [<Job Title A>, <Job Title B>]\n\n*** FINAL OUTPUT STRUCTURE ***\n\nYou must return exactly one JSON object with the following structure:\n\n{\n  \"req_cand_matching_criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"requisitionId\": \"<REQUISITION_ID_A>\",\n      \"ReqTitle\": \"<REQUISITION_TITLE_A>\",\n      \"SearchCriteria\": \"Skills: [<Skill A>, <Skill B>]; Degree: [<Degree Name>], JobTitle: [<Job Title A>]\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requisitionId\": \"<REQUISITION_ID_B>\",\n      \"ReqTitle\": \"<REQUISITION_TITLE_B>\",\n      \"SearchCriteria\": \"Skills: [<Skill C>, <Skill D>]; Degree: [<Degree Name>]\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n*** BEGIN GENERATION ***"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"req_cand_matching_criteria\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"requisitionId\": {\n            \"type\": [\n              \"string\",\n              \"number\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"ReqTitle\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"SearchCriteria\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"additionalProperties\": true\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"req_cand_matching_criteria\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}\n"
        },
